; grid_scan_scales_with_extent (QUI-1056): pins the step cost of the four
; grid scans, whose work scales with an extent the program chooses.
;
; A 12-variable model is gridded 3x4, so a row scan touches 4 cells and a
; column scan touches 3. Each cell is charged GRID_CELL_STEPS (3), per
; spec/xqvm/METERING.md. The two shapes are exercised in the same program
; so a divergence in either axis shows up as a single step-count mismatch.
;
; ROWFIND searches for a value the row does not hold, so the scan runs to
; the end; COLFIND searches for one the column holds in its first cell, so
; the scan short-circuits. Both are charged for their full extent, and this
; vector is what makes that normative rather than incidental.

PUSH 12
BQMX r0

PUSH 0
PUSH 7
SETLINE r0

PUSH 3
PUSH 4
RESIZE r0

; row 0 spans cells 0..4 -- 4 * 3 = 12 steps on top of the base cost.
PUSH 0
ROWSUM r0
STOW r1

; column 0 spans cells 0, 4, 8 -- 3 * 3 = 9 steps on top of the base cost.
PUSH 0
COLSUM r0
STOW r2

; scans all 4 cells of row 0 and finds nothing: charged 12, returns -1.
PUSH 0
PUSH 99
ROWFIND r0
STOW r3

; matches at the first of column 0's 3 cells: still charged 9, returns 0.
PUSH 0
PUSH 7
COLFIND r0
STOW r4

PUSH 0
OUTPUT r1
PUSH 1
OUTPUT r2
PUSH 2
OUTPUT r3
PUSH 3
OUTPUT r4
HALT
